<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Rashid of Morocco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1631–<a href="/years/1672">1672</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Moulay al-Rashid, Moulay Rashid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Rashid was the first sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaouite-dynasty">Alaouite dynasty of Morocco</a>, ruling from 1666 to 1672. Starting from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tafilalt">Tafilalt</a>, he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> in 1666, crushed the Dila'iyya in 1668, took the corsair towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabat">Rabat</a>, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> in 1669 and subdued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tazeroualt">Tazeroualt</a> in 1670, reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> after the Saadi collapse. His brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moulay-ismail">Moulay Ismail</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-rashid-of-morocco.jpg" alt="Al-Rashid of Morocco" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicolas de Larmessin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cherif_Muley-Arxid.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
